<title>UK: Canada's Moore to buy Colleagues.</title>
<headline>Canada's Moore to buy Colleagues.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British marketing services company Colleagues Group Plc announced on Wednesday it had received an recommended a takeover offer of 95 pence a share from Canadian business products group Moore Corporation.</p>
<p>The offer valued the entire share capital of Colleagues at 21,6 million stg.  </p>
<p>The share price of Colleagues shot up 21 pence to 98-1/2 in early Wednesday trade.</p>
<p>The price reflects a premium of 48 percent to the closing mid-price of the company on March 3, 1997, the last dealing day before it announced that it was in talks for a merger.</p>
<p>The price represents a multiple of 31.7 times Colleagues earnings per share for the year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
